# ABC Institute of Technology – College Handbook 2026

## 1. General Information

ABC Institute of Technology was established in 2005. It is located in New Delhi, India. The institution offers undergraduate and postgraduate programs in engineering, computer applications, management, and applied sciences.

The college operates from Monday to Saturday. Normal academic working hours are 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM.

The academic year is divided into two semesters:
- Odd Semester: August to December
- Even Semester: January to May

The summer vacation generally takes place during June and July.

## 2. Departments and Courses

### Computer Science and Engineering (CSE)

The CSE department offers a four-year Bachelor of Technology (B.Tech) program.

Major subjects include:
- Data Structures and Algorithms
- Database Management Systems
- Operating Systems
- Computer Networks
- Artificial Intelligence
- Machine Learning
- Software Engineering
- Cloud Computing

The department has 12 faculty members and approximately 480 students.

### Information Technology (IT)

The IT department focuses on software development, information security, and modern computing technologies.

Major subjects include:
- Web Development
- Java Programming
- Python Programming
- Cyber Security
- Distributed Systems
- Mobile Application Development

The department has 8 faculty members and approximately 320 students.

### Electronics and Communication Engineering (ECE)

The ECE department focuses on electronics, communication systems, and embedded technologies.

Major subjects include:
- Digital Electronics
- Microprocessors
- Signal Processing
- Communication Systems
- Embedded Systems

## 3. Admission Policy

Students seeking admission to B.Tech programs must have completed their 10+2 education with Physics and Mathematics as compulsory subjects.

Admission is primarily based on entrance examination performance and applicable university admission guidelines.

Documents required during admission:
1. Class 10 marksheet.
2. Class 12 marksheet.
3. Entrance examination scorecard.
4. Transfer certificate.
5. Migration certificate, if applicable.
6. Recent passport-sized photographs.
7. Identity proof.

The admission office operates from 10:00 AM to 4:00 PM on working days.

## 4. Attendance Policy

Students must maintain at least 75% attendance in each subject to be eligible for university examinations.

Attendance is calculated separately for every subject.

Students with attendance below 75% may be detained from appearing in the respective semester examination, subject to university regulations.

Medical leave applications must be submitted with supporting medical documents to the department coordinator.

## 5. Examination Policy

Each semester consists of:
- Internal Assessment: 30 marks.
- End Semester Examination: 70 marks.

The minimum passing marks are 40% overall, subject to applicable university examination regulations.

Internal assessment includes:
- Assignments.
- Class tests.
- Practical evaluations.
- Attendance and participation where applicable.

Students must carry their university identity cards during examinations.

Mobile phones and unauthorized electronic devices are prohibited inside examination halls.

## 6. Library Facilities

The central library operates from 8:30 AM to 6:00 PM, Monday through Saturday.

Students can borrow up to four books simultaneously.

The standard borrowing period is 14 days.

A late return fine of ₹5 per book per day is charged.

Students must present their college identity cards to borrow books.

The library provides:
- Technical books.
- Research journals.
- Newspapers.
- Digital learning resources.
- Previous semester question papers.

## 7. Hostel Facilities

The college provides separate hostel accommodation for male and female students.

Hostel facilities include:
- Wi-Fi connectivity.
- Laundry facilities.
- Common recreation rooms.
- Mess facilities.
- 24-hour security.

Hostel entry timing is 9:00 PM on weekdays and 10:00 PM on weekends.

Students requiring permission to stay outside the hostel overnight must obtain approval from the hostel warden.

## 8. Scholarship Programs

The college provides several scholarship opportunities.

### Merit Scholarship

Students scoring above 90% in their qualifying examination may apply for a merit scholarship.

The scholarship covers 50% of the annual tuition fee.

### Financial Assistance Scholarship

Students from economically weaker sections may apply for financial assistance.

Eligibility is determined based on family income and supporting documents.

### Sports Scholarship

Students who have represented their state or country in recognized sports competitions may apply.

The scholarship amount depends on the level of achievement and institutional approval.

## 9. Placement Cell

The Training and Placement Cell coordinates campus recruitment activities.

Its responsibilities include:
- Organizing placement drives.
- Conducting aptitude training.
- Arranging technical workshops.
- Providing interview preparation.
- Connecting students with recruiting companies.

Students must register with the placement cell to participate in campus recruitment.

Companies may establish additional eligibility criteria based on academic performance, active backlogs, and technical skills.

